---
const title = "How a simple Raspberry Pi computer got me into the best hobby I've ever had";
const description =
  'A Raspberry Pi 4, Home Assistant, a few Broadlink blasters and some Shelly relays turned a 15-year-old AC and a dumb switch into a smart home my parents actually use.';
const canonical = 'https://adityanihlani.com/blog/raspberry-pi-smart-home/';

const stack = [
  { n: '01', k: 'The brain', v: 'Raspberry Pi 4B · 8 GB' },
  { n: '02', k: 'The software', v: 'Home Assistant OS' },
  { n: '03', k: 'The AC whisperers', v: 'Broadlink + SmartIR' },
  { n: '04', k: 'The muscle', v: 'Shelly 2PM · Gen3' },
  { n: '05', k: 'The front door', v: 'Apple HomeKit + Siri' },
];
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="article" />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:url" content={canonical} />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://adityanihlani.com/images/pi4-top.jpg" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <link
      rel="icon"
      href="data:image/svg+xml,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 16 16'><text y='13' font-size='13'>A</text></svg>"
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,300..700;1,9..144,300..600&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=JetBrains+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="progress" aria-hidden="true"><span id="bar"></span></div>

    <header class="top">
      <a class="mark" href="/">Aditya Nihlani</a>
      <span class="tag">Notes · Vol. 01</span>
    </header>

    <main>
      <!-- HERO -->
      <section class="hero">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Home automation · Essay 01</p>
        <h1>
          How a simple <em>Raspberry Pi</em> got me into the best hobby I’ve ever had
        </h1>
        <p class="dek">
          One little green board, one SD card, and a house that slowly started to listen.
        </p>
        <p class="byline">
          <span>By Aditya Nihlani</span><i></i><span>5 min read</span><i></i><span>Oct 2026</span>
        </p>
      </section>

      <figure class="hero-img">
        <div class="glow"></div>
        <img
          src="/images/pi4-top.jpg"
          alt="Top-down photo of a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B circuit board"
          width="1920"
          height="1282"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
        <figcaption>
          The Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. Mine is the 8&nbsp;GB one.
          <span class="credit">Photo: Laserlicht / Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <article class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          I bought a computer. A real one, with RAM and storage and everything, from a shop, at a
          price that didn’t make me wince.
        </p>

        <p>
          That sentence is going to sound strange in a few years. I picked up my Raspberry Pi kit
          from Robu back in the golden age, <em>before the AI explosion</em>, when ordinary people
          could still just buy a computer. Today it feels like we’ve wandered into a cyberpunk
          novel: scavenging for used parts, hunting down memory like it’s contraband, assembling
          machines from whatever the gods of the secondary market provide.
        </p>

        <p>
          I’m glad I got in when I did. The kit came with the official power adapter, the HDMI
          cable and a proper enclosure, and the board inside it was a <strong>Raspberry Pi 4B with
          8&nbsp;GB of RAM</strong>. I had no plan. I just wanted to see what it could do.
        </p>

        <div class="chip-row" role="list">
          <span role="listitem">Raspberry Pi 4B</span>
          <span role="listitem">8 GB RAM</span>
          <span role="listitem">Official PSU</span>
          <span role="listitem">Official case</span>
          <span role="listitem">Micro-HDMI cable</span>
        </div>

        <h2><span class="num">01</span> The SD card that blew my mind</h2>

        <p>
          The first thing I did was flash <strong>Home Assistant</strong> onto the SD card that
          came with the Pi. I expected a blank dashboard and an afternoon of reading docs.
        </p>

        <p>
          Instead, it <em>already knew things</em>.
        </p>

        <p>
          Within moments Home Assistant had sniffed out the smart devices on my network, the
          handful I’d forgotten I even owned. The <strong>bedside lamp</strong>. The{" "}<strong>TV</strong>. They just appeared, each one with a name and a toggle, as if the
          house had been quietly waiting for someone to ask.
        </p>

        <figure class="shot">
          <div class="browser">
            <div class="chrome"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
            <img
              src="/images/ha-dashboard.png"
              alt="Home Assistant demo dashboard showing rooms, lights, climate and energy cards"
              width="1596"
              height="923"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            Home Assistant’s dashboard, a living map of your house.
            <span class="credit">Home Assistant demo · Apache License 2.0 · via Wikimedia Commons</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <blockquote>
          I had a computer on my desk that understood my house better than I did.
        </blockquote>

        <p>That was the hook. I’ve not been able to put it down since.</p>

        <h2><span class="num">02</span> Teaching a 15-year-old AC new tricks</h2>

        <p>
          Next I looked at the least smart things in the house: our aging air conditioners. Fifteen
          years old, plastic remotes, absolutely zero connectivity.
        </p>

        <p>
          So I fell down the rabbit hole. I learnt about <strong>SmartIR</strong>, bought a few{" "}<strong>Broadlink</strong> IR controllers, and, somehow, after plenty of trial and
          error, made them work. Then came the part I’m proudest of: I bridged everything into{" "}<strong>Apple HomeKit</strong>.
        </p>

        <div class="flow" aria-label="How the AC control chain fits together">
          <div class="node"><b>Siri / Home app</b><small>the voice</small></div>
          <div class="arrow"></div>
          <div class="node"><b>Home Assistant</b><small>on the Pi</small></div>
          <div class="arrow"></div>
          <div class="node"><b>Broadlink</b><small>IR blaster</small></div>
          <div class="arrow"></div>
          <div class="node"><b>15-year-old AC</b><small>still going</small></div>
        </div>

        <p>
          A fifteen-year-old air conditioner, running through Apple HomeKit. <em>Locally</em>. No
          cloud, no subscription, no waiting for a server in another country to wake up.
        </p>

        <aside class="callout">
          <p class="callout-k">The part that actually mattered</p>
          <p>
            My parents are 60. They don’t care about integrations or YAML. They care that “Hey
            Siri, turn on the AC” just works, and it does, every single time. The impact was so
            big that <strong>we lost the AC remotes</strong> and nobody noticed. Nobody uses them
            anymore.
          </p>
        </aside>

        <h2><span class="num">03</span> Meet the Shellys</h2>

        <p>
          Then I discovered <strong>Shelly</strong>. I ordered a few straight from their official
          website: the <strong>3rd-gen 2PM</strong> relays, tiny modules that hide behind a switch
          and quietly make it clever.
        </p>

        <p>
          That was the final unlock. Suddenly my dumb switches and dumb lights were joining in too,
          all of them showing up in Apple HomeKit like they’d been smart all along. No new
          fixtures, no ripping out walls, just a small box behind a plate and a house that suddenly
          had opinions.
        </p>

        <div class="stack">
          {
            stack.map((s) => (
              <div class="row">
                <span class="n">{s.n}</span>
                <span class="k">{s.k}</span>
                <span class="v">{s.v}</span>
              </div>
            ))
          }
        </div>

        <h2><span class="num">04</span> A very Stark kind of feeling</h2>

        <p>
          Very soon, my house had become a smart home. A <strong>cheap</strong> one. A{" "}<strong>reliable</strong> one. One that runs on my own hardware, on my own network, doing
          what I tell it to.
        </p>

        <p>
          It became the best hobby I’ve ever had. And I’ll admit it: at some point, standing in a
          dark room, saying a sentence out loud and watching the lights answer, I felt a little
          like <strong>Tony Stark</strong>.
        </p>

        <h2><span class="num">05</span> And then we moved</h2>

        <p>
          The timing turned out to be perfect. I was about to move into a new house, and everything
          I’d learnt on the old one, every relay, every quirk, every late-night “why won’t this
          pair”, was about to matter. A cheap little computer had been quietly training me for the
          real thing.
        </p>

        <p class="closing">
          That’s a story for the next post.
        </p>

        <div class="end-mark" aria-hidden="true">◆</div>
      </article>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <a href="/">Aditya Nihlani</a>
      <span>Built with Astro · Runs on a Pi, probably</span>
    </footer>

    <script is:inline>
      const bar = document.getElementById('bar');
      const update = () => {
        const h = document.documentElement;
        const p = h.scrollTop / Math.max(1, h.scrollHeight - h.clientHeight);
        bar.style.transform = 'scaleX(' + Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p)) + ')';
      };
      addEventListener('scroll', update, { passive: true });
      update();

      const io = new IntersectionObserver(
        (es) => es.forEach((e) => e.isIntersecting && (e.target.classList.add('in'), io.unobserve(e.target))),
        { threshold: 0.12 }
      );
      document.querySelectorAll('.prose > *, .shot, .stack .row, .flow').forEach((el) => {
        el.classList.add('reveal');
        io.observe(el);
      });
    </script>

    <style is:global>
      :root {
        --bg: #0b0d0c;
        --bg2: #121513;
        --fg: #ece9e1;
        --muted: #8d9490;
        --line: rgba(236, 233, 225, 0.1);
        --accent: #7bd88f;
        --accent2: #e9b96e;
        --serif: 'Fraunces', 'Iowan Old Style', Georgia, serif;
        --sans: 'Inter', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
        --mono: 'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {
        :root {
          --bg: #f6f3ec;
          --bg2: #ece7db;
          --fg: #16191a;
          --muted: #6a716d;
          --line: rgba(22, 25, 26, 0.12);
          --accent: #1f7a3c;
          --accent2: #a8641a;
        }
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--fg);
        font-family: var(--sans);
        font-size: 17px;
        line-height: 1.75;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        background-image:
          radial-gradient(60rem 32rem at 80% -8%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 14%, transparent), transparent 70%),
          radial-gradient(40rem 26rem at -10% 4%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent2) 9%, transparent), transparent 70%);
        background-repeat: no-repeat;
      }
      ::selection { background: var(--accent); color: #07110a; }

      .progress { position: fixed; inset: 0 0 auto 0; height: 2px; z-index: 50; }
      .progress span {
        display: block; height: 100%; transform-origin: 0 50%; transform: scaleX(0);
        background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2));
      }

      .top {
        max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem 1.5rem 0;
        display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;
        font-size: 0.85rem;
      }
      .mark { color: var(--fg); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
      .tag { font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; }

      .hero { max-width: 880px; margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 6.5rem) 1.5rem 2.5rem; }
      .eyebrow {
        display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.74rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
      }
      .dot { width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 var(--accent); animation: pulse 2.4s infinite; }
      @keyframes pulse { 70% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 10px transparent; } 100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 transparent; } }

      h1 {
        font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 400; margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 6.4vw, 4.6rem); line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -0.025em;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 144;
      }
      h1 em { font-style: italic; color: var(--accent); }
      .dek { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.4vw, 1.5rem); line-height: 1.45; color: var(--muted); margin: 1.6rem 0 0; max-width: 34ch; font-weight: 300; }
      .byline { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 0.9rem; margin: 2.2rem 0 0; font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--muted); }
      .byline i { width: 3px; height: 3px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--muted); }
      .byline span:first-child { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 500; }

      .hero-img { position: relative; max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 1.5rem; }
      .hero-img .glow {
        position: absolute; inset: 8% 12% -6%; background: radial-gradient(closest-side, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, transparent), transparent);
        filter: blur(50px); opacity: 0.55; z-index: 0;
      }
      .hero-img img {
        position: relative; z-index: 1; display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 20px;
        border: 1px solid var(--line); box-shadow: 0 40px 80px -30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.7);
        aspect-ratio: 16 / 8; object-fit: cover;
      }
      figcaption { position: relative; z-index: 1; margin-top: 0.9rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; }
      .credit { display: block; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.68rem; opacity: 0.75; margin-top: 0.2rem; }

      .prose { max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; padding: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem) 1.5rem 4rem; }
      .prose p { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 88%, transparent); }
      .prose strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 600; }
      .prose em { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 1.04em; }
      .lede { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 1.75rem) !important; line-height: 1.42; color: var(--fg) !important; font-weight: 350; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
      .lede::first-letter {
        float: left; font-size: 4.4em; line-height: 0.82; padding: 0.08em 0.1em 0 0; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 500;
      }

      .prose h2 {
        font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 4vw, 2.3rem); line-height: 1.15;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 4rem 0 1.4rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.6rem;
      }
      .num { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--accent); }
      .num::after { content: ''; display: inline-block; width: 2.6rem; height: 1px; background: var(--accent); vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 0.7rem; opacity: 0.6; }

      .chip-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
      .chip-row span {
        font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.74rem; padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; border-radius: 999px;
        border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg2); color: var(--muted);
      }

      blockquote {
        margin: 3rem -1rem; padding: 0.5rem 0 0.5rem 1.6rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
        font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-weight: 300; font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 3.4vw, 1.95rem); line-height: 1.35; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }

      .shot { max-width: 1000px; margin: 3rem 0; position: relative; }
      .browser { border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: #1b1d1c; box-shadow: 0 30px 70px -30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6); }
      .chrome { display: flex; gap: 6px; padding: 10px 12px; background: #1b1d1c; }
      .chrome i { width: 9px; height: 9px; border-radius: 50%; background: #444a47; }
      .browser img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }

      .flow { display: flex; align-items: stretch; gap: 0; margin: 2.4rem 0 2.6rem; }
      .node {
        flex: 1; padding: 1rem 0.9rem; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px; background: var(--bg2);
        display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.2rem; text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.3;
      }
      .node small { color: var(--muted); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.66rem; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
      .arrow { width: 26px; align-self: center; height: 1px; background: var(--accent); position: relative; flex: none; }
      .arrow::after { content: ''; position: absolute; right: 0; top: -3px; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-top: 1px solid var(--accent); border-right: 1px solid var(--accent); transform: rotate(45deg); }

      .callout {
        margin: 2.4rem 0; padding: 1.6rem 1.7rem; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid var(--line);
        background: linear-gradient(160deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 11%, var(--bg2)), var(--bg2));
      }
      .callout p { margin: 0 !important; }
      .callout .callout-k { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent) !important; margin-bottom: 0.7rem !important; }

      .stack { margin: 2.6rem 0 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
      .stack .row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr auto; gap: 1rem; align-items: baseline; padding: 1rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); transition: padding 0.25s ease; }
      .stack .row:hover { padding-left: 0.6rem; }
      .stack .n { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--accent); }
      .stack .k { font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 1.15rem; }
      .stack .v { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.76rem; color: var(--muted); text-align: right; }

      .closing { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 1.3rem !important; color: var(--accent) !important; margin-top: 2.4rem !important; }
      .end-mark { text-align: center; color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 3rem; letter-spacing: 1em; }

      footer {
        max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.5rem 3rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
        display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted);
      }
      footer a { color: var(--fg); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500; }

      .reveal { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(14px); transition: opacity 0.7s ease, transform 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.7, 0.2, 1); }
      .reveal.in { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
        .reveal { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; }
        .dot { animation: none; }
      }

      @media (max-width: 640px) {
        body { font-size: 16px; }
        blockquote { margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; }
        .flow { flex-direction: column; }
        .arrow { width: 1px; height: 22px; align-self: center; }
        .arrow::after { right: -3px; top: auto; bottom: 0; transform: rotate(135deg); }
        .stack .row { grid-template-columns: 2.4rem 1fr; }
        .stack .v { grid-column: 2; text-align: left; }
        .hero-img img { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
        .top .tag { display: none; }
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
